    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "An ACE inhibitor (ACEi) or angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) is recommended for patients with T1D or T2D who have hypertension and albuminuria, titrated to the maximum antihypertensive or highest tolerated dose." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "An ACE inhibitor (ACEi) or angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) is recommended for patients with T1D or T2D who have hypertension and albuminuria, titrated to the maximum antihypertensive or highest tolerated dose." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/ada-kdigo-consensus-report-diabetes-ckd-diabetes-care-2022> .

